# ABSENKOK — kiosk runtime environment
#
# This template documents the two values the Flutter app reads at runtime via
# `flutter_dotenv` (see `lib/main.dart`). The real values are baked into the
# APK as a bundled asset by the GitHub Actions release workflow — the .env
# file is NEVER committed to source control. Use this template if you fork
# the repo and need to rebuild the kiosk against a different Supabase project.
#
# Both values are public-by-design for a Flutter app talking to Supabase:
#   - SUPABASE_URL is hard-coded into the bundled `.env` asset and trivially
#     extractable from any APK.
#   - SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is a JWT signed by Supabase that exposes only what
#     RLS policies allow. It is meant to ship in the client.
#
# DO NOT add SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY here. The kiosk does not use it. Any
# build that bundles the service-role key would give every kiosk operator
# full database bypass authority.
#
# To rebuild against your own Supabase project, copy this file to `.env` at
# the repo root before `flutter build apk`.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key
